firefox: hold the description of the theme to one line

The card of about:addons shows the description under the name of the
theme. The sheet of the page holds a closed card to one line: it sets
white-space to nowrap and text-overflow to ellipsis. A card cuts a
longer description at the width of the list.

Every theme that Firefox ships holds one short sentence there. The
light theme holds 34 characters and the dark theme holds 33
characters. The longest of the shipped lines holds 68 characters. The
description of this theme held 242 characters over three sentences, and
the card cut it.

The change sits on the branch work/firefox-theme of the local tree, as
commit 13 of 14. The branch holds those fourteen commits above the head of
work/gtk4-theme, which merge request !15 on system/qtcurve holds. The fork
wyn/qtcurve holds work/firefox-theme. Merge request !29 on system/qtcurve
holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/firefox/check/assert-ff-manifest.cmake b/firefox/check/assert-ff-manifest.cmake
index 957f0879..66142298 100644
--- a/firefox/check/assert-ff-manifest.cmake
+++ b/firefox/check/assert-ff-manifest.cmake
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 # know without a word, so a name outside the list paints nothing.
 #
 # The manifest must also hold a description and an author, which the card of
-# about:addons shows under the name of the theme. The run then doctors five
+# about:addons shows under the name of the theme. The run then doctors six
 # copies of the manifest, and it fails if the check passes a copy. cmake -P
 # takes the four names as -D definitions, and the usage message below names
 # them.
@@ -69,6 +69,18 @@ function(qtc_check text fault)
       return()
     endif()
   endforeach()
+  # The card of a closed add-on holds one line: aboutaddons.css of Firefox
+  # sets white-space to nowrap over the contents and text-overflow to
+  # ellipsis over the description. A longer line takes a cut. The bound of 68
+  # characters is the longest description that Firefox ships, which the
+  # default theme holds.
+  string(JSON line GET "${text}" description)
+  string(LENGTH "${line}" wide)
+  if(wide GREATER 68)
+    set("${fault}" "the description holds ${wide} characters, over 68"
+      PARENT_SCOPE)
+    return()
+  endif()
   foreach(half theme dark_theme)
     if(half STREQUAL "theme")
       set(scheme light)
@@ -150,6 +162,12 @@ string(REPLACE "\"description\":" "\"qtc_no_description\":" qtc_line_copy
   "${qtc_text}")
 qtc_control(description "${qtc_line_copy}")
 
+# The control below pads the description past the bound of the card.
+string(REGEX REPLACE "\"description\": \"[^\"]*\""
+  "\"description\": \"A theme that paints the window, the tabs and the address bar in the colours of QtCurve.\""
+  qtc_long_copy "${qtc_text}")
+qtc_control(length "${qtc_long_copy}")
+
 string(REPLACE "\"author\":" "\"qtc_no_author\":" qtc_who_copy "${qtc_text}")
 qtc_control(author "${qtc_who_copy}")
 
diff --git a/firefox/writer/manifest.cpp b/firefox/writer/manifest.cpp
index f215376e..3ce9e9f5 100644
--- a/firefox/writer/manifest.cpp
+++ b/firefox/writer/manifest.cpp
@@ -43,11 +43,7 @@ const char *const themeName = "QtCurve";
  * The line under the name on the card of about:addons. The card of a theme
  * holds the name, this line and the preview image, and it holds no icon.
  */
-const char *const themeDescription =
-    "This theme paints the Firefox window, the tabs and the address bar in"
-    " the colours of QtCurve. On its own it uses the default QtCurve colours,"
-    " light or dark to match your system. With QtCurve on Linux, the colours"
-    " can follow your own settings.";
+const char *const themeDescription = "A theme with the colours of QtCurve.";
 
 /** The author of the add-on, which the open card of about:addons shows. */
 const char *const themeAuthor = "Wyn Sun";
